  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"rschema_0439\" consists of five tables: User, Merchant, Recycling_Request, Transaction_Order, and Order_Review.\nThe User table is used to store user information. It includes columns for Password, Phone_Number, User_ID (which is the primary key), User_Name, and WeChat_ID.\nThe Merchant table is used to store merchant information. It includes columns for Address, Contact_Information, Merchant_Account (which is the primary key), and Password.\nThe Recycling_Request table is used to store recycling request information. It includes columns for Order_ID (which is the primary key), Recycling_Location, Recycling_Time, Request_Time, and Request_User (which is a foreign key referencing the User_ID in the User table).\nThe Transaction_Order table is used to store transaction order information. It includes columns for Accepting_Merchant (which is a foreign key referencing the Merchant_Account in the Merchant table), Order_ID (which is the primary key and also a foreign key referencing the Order_ID in the Recycling_Request table), Order_Status, Payment_Amount, and Payment_Method.\nThe Order_Review table is used to store order review information. It includes columns for Order_ID (which is the primary key and also a foreign key referencing the Order_ID in the Recycling_Request table), Rating, Review_Content.\nAll columns allow null values except for Request_User in the Recycling_Request table and Accepting_Merchant in the Transaction_Order table, which are not null. The database schema ensures referential integrity by maintaining foreign key relationships between the tables.",
  "gold_question": "\"The system is designed for a waste collection platform, requiring management of both user and merchant accounts, and allowing users to register and log in via mobile phone number or WeChat. Users can post recycling requests, including details of the waste items such as type, quantity, location, and time. Merchants can then accept and fulfill these orders. The system must record the status and payment information of each order and provide a rating function for users to grade and comment on the service after order completion. Administrators can access all user and merchant information and perform necessary maintenance operations.\"",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0439.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0439\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `wechat_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `merchant` (\n  `merchant_account` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`merchant_account`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `recycling_request` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recycling_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recycling_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `request_user` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `recycling_request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`request_user`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transaction_order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `accepting_merchant` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_method` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `recycling_request` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `transaction_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`accepting_merchant`) REFERENCES `merchant` (`merchant_account`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `order_review` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_review_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `recycling_request` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
